# Agent envs
PORT=8080
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6

# Ceiling on a single /invocations body, in characters. The BFF's own MAX_MESSAGE_LENGTH already
# bounds what reaches here and the BFF is the runtime's only caller, so this is the ceiling that
# holds if anything ever invokes the runtime directly. Default 20000.
# MAX_BODY_LENGTH=20000

# ── Conversation memory ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The AgentCore Memory resource conversations are recorded in, set by
# infra/src/stacks/agent-stack.ts. Left unset here on purpose: `npm run dev` then answers every turn
# without history and records nothing, which keeps local development free of a managed resource.
# Encryption and retention are properties of that resource, not of this process.
# AGENTCORE_MEMORY_ID=my_project_memory-XXXXXXXXXX

# How many past messages are replayed into a new turn. Each turn re-sends the context it is given,
# so an uncapped history makes a long conversation cost more with every message. Default 40.
# MEMORY_MAX_MESSAGES=40

# ── Content guardrail ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A Bedrock guardrail id and version. Both must be set for the guardrail to apply — a half-configured
# pair is treated as absent rather than as an error, so a demo without one still runs. The deployment
# gate (infra/src/config.ts) requires them under DEPLOY_PROFILE=pilot and prod, where "no content
# filter" stops being an acceptable answer.
# BEDROCK_GUARDRAIL_ID=abcd1234efgh
# BEDROCK_GUARDRAIL_VERSION=1

# ── Telemetry ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Strands Agent emits spans and token/tool metrics on its own; they reach a no-op provider until
# an OTLP endpoint is configured. Setting this — the standard OTel variable, so a collector that
# already sets it needs nothing here — turns on tracing and metrics export.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=my-project-agent

# Disables TLS certificate verification for the WHOLE process — the calls to Bedrock included, not
# just the one connection you had in mind. Left commented on purpose: this file is meant to be
# copied to .env verbatim. Uncomment only if you know exactly which connection needs it, and put it
# back afterwards.
# NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0

# Invoke script envs (npm run invoke:bedrock)
# AWS_REGION is already defined above, but you can override it here if needed.
# The script signs with SigV4 from your ambient AWS profile — the only way into the runtime, which
# carries no JWT authorizer. Your profile needs bedrock-agentcore:InvokeAgentRuntime on this ARN.
AGENT_RUNTIME_ARN=arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:us-east-1:YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID:runtime/my-agent-service-XXXXXXXXXX
